"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T02:39:16-07:00","id":642778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=642040#post642040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No gonna lie, that last one sounded <i>a lot</i> like an anti-LGBT ad. Which, when you think about it, was probably the intent. Although, I think the comparison is less apt for WoD vampires, seeing as Kindred are objectively monstrous (or at the very least, feral) on some level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampires in general make a terrible metaphor for LGBT people. first and foremost vampires are literally recruited and many of them chose to become vampires. and as you mentioned, vampires legitmatly are predatory and dangerous and lets not even getting into passing their condition along by exchanging blood.<br /> <br /> in fact its probably a good idea not to use any of the splats for LGBT people. for example, if it must be explained why using Changelings: People who were stolen <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">by faeries</span></span></span> and twisted into something literally non human and must struggle to hold on to their sanity, would be homophobic, well this link would probably help: <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/UnfortunateImplications\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...teImplications</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T10:14:08-07:00","id":644371,"title":"","content":"I myself am Bisexual and Genderqueer, I really didn't see that in that commercial<br /> <br /> I don't want them living in my neighborhood- Well duh. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> As soon as one moves in, property values go down all over the place- With vampires as a known and people not wanting to deal with them, its probably true.<br /> <br /> Just don't feel safe at night anymore- Ummm Bloodthirsty Vampires much. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> I don't want them anywhere near my kids- I kinda wouldn't either. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Children see this lifestyle and maybe want to imitate it- Remember that Children includes teens, and maybe they even want to enter it, cuz quite a few people see vamps as sexy, Hell Vampires probably aren't even real and people imitate it now... o.o<br /> <br /> They're just so unnatural- They're Undead, I'd say that's pretty unnatural.<br /> <br /> Should we just go and let them do whatever they want? Absolutely Not- Like drinking people's blood, killing them, turning them into blood dolls.<br /> <br /> They make me scared- Me too lil girl. Me too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T10:43:32-07:00","id":644406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=644371#post644371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I myself am Bisexual and Genderqueer, I really didn't see that in that commercial</div> </div> </div> </div>It just struck me as being similar to a lot of the arguments that people use to discriminate against LGBTEtc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T11:42:40-07:00","id":644452,"title":"","content":"Well, it is obviously a comparison. But NOT a metaphor for Gender-whatever people. It is a metaphor for the ads themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T12:24:24-07:00","id":644489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=644452#post644452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a metaphor for the ads themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I can fully agree with. I get rather upset by people who are like that (as my parents are x.x), I'd probably be one of the people voting for the Rights of Vampires and other Supernaturals, even If I become more afraid of going out at night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Though with rights and recognition comes the force of Law. There would probably be those in said Supernatural societies willing to work against the crimes of their people, to Police them so that the whole of their kind wouldn't be fought against","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 08-29-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:11:49-07:00","id":644562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=644489#post644489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Though with rights and recognition comes the force of Law. There would probably be those in said Supernatural societies willing to work against the crimes of their people, to Police them so that the whole of their kind wouldn't be fought against</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but think that such individuals would inspire countless supernatural police procedurals. And also, Law and Order would be pretty much forced to make a hasty, poorly-researched and written episodes about supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T13:55:05-07:00","id":644610,"title":"","content":"In that kind of world would Hunters then be considered Vigilantes against Supernaturals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 08-29-2015, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:27:40-07:00","id":644624,"title":"","content":"I think hunters would be revealed along with the rest of the World of Darkness. Task Force Valkyrie would be accepted eventually, there would be a huge scandal due to the Posse Comitatus act and they'd have to be fully set up as a branch of the National Guard or, more likely, a branch of the Department of Homeland Security, providing it isn't already. Local and state governments would probably operate something smaller scale, specially trained officers similar to those from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_Valley_(TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">Death Valley</a> series. Obviously there would be all sorts of legal weirdnesses about whether vampires were still people, what to do about changelings and their fetches, prometheans and so forth. The Malleus Maleficarum would probably be able to bring a lot into the Church but they'd probably find their license to go around wherever they want hindered in certain places. The Ascended Ones would probably be targeted by ISIS and other extremists, and not be received by the other side very well either.<br /> <br /> I guess a lot would depend on how it happened and when it happened, but I believe eventually there would be a system in place for hunters, whether it involves simply absolving them of crimes due to technicalities or having them become part of some legally recognized militia with, ideally, a lot of oversight. That's just in America, though, and stuff would be crazy everywhere for a long time if the Masquerade was just torn down overnight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:39:21-07:00","id":644631,"title":"","content":"Well I was talking Tier 1 Hunters, I figured there would be all kinds of weirdness or acceptance for different Hunter Conspiracies and Compacts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:42:56-07:00","id":644636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=644631#post644631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I was talking Tier 1 Hunters, I figured there would be all kinds of weirdness or acceptance for different Hunter Conspiracies and Compacts</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah they were the ones who'd have the system in place. Depending on how things went, either you'd get a pass because no one wants a vampire dating their daughter, or the vampire rights associations would make sure you spent the rest of your life in jail.<br /> <br /> Though I would sincerely hope we'd use our new found illumination to better our rehabilitation of criminals and others.<br /> <br /> All in all it makes me glad the standard setting uses the Masquerade. It would be hard to exult in being monster when you have to live with the same constraints as everyone else.<br /> <br /> But it's fun to think about the pop culture that would spring up, I just have a harder time thinking of the wider reactions.<br /> <br /> Could Count Dracula sue to get the rights to his name? Would Disney start buying up Changeling stories? Would you have to get a permit to perform Siskur-Dah?<br /> <br /> And it's just amusing to think that the groups that are ostensibly antagonists would be well received. What corporation <i>wouldn't</i> want to hire a Seer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-29-2015, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T19:04:39-07:00","id":644823,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=malonkey1]<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I can't help but think that such individuals would inspire countless supernatural police procedurals. And also, Law and Order would be pretty much forced to make a hasty, poorly-researched and written episodes about supernaturals.[</span></span></span>/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Maybe that'll finally take them off the air...or more likely force them to do a much more sympathetic episode to whatever Subculture of The Week is the SCARY NOT AUDIENCE that episode later, on pain of blackmail. <br /> <br /> And the sad part is, that blackmail's probably going to be one of their better written episodes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=644636#post644636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's just amusing to think that the groups that are ostensibly antagonists would be well received. What corporation <i>wouldn't</i> want to hire a Seer?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;As a gesture of solidarity, please do not infringe upon the religious beliefs of our new business consultant, Dr. Gaius R. Kralomoc. What he does with his time, friends, congregation, and sacrificial animals is entirely his personal business, and does not completely impact your personal fortunes. He is not a Satanist, simply a man born with unique abilities and for whom those abilities hold spiritual significance. Please do not spread rumors about his organization, his power, or his tendency to greet other people by informing them to lay prostrate before him. We hope that we will give in a nurturing and supportive environment, where his laugh is answered with chuckles of our own, rather than terror and hopes that he is not laughing about something involving our own lives.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T03:23:23-07:00","id":645210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=644624#post644624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think hunters would be revealed along with the rest of the World of Darkness. Task Force Valkyrie would be accepted eventually, there would be a huge scandal due to the Posse Comitatus act and they'd have to be fully set up as a branch of the National Guard or, more likely, a branch of the Department of Homeland Security, providing it isn't already. Local and state governments would probably operate something smaller scale, specially trained officers similar to those from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_Valley_(TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">Death Valley</a> series. Obviously there would be all sorts of legal weirdnesses about whether vampires were still people, what to do about changelings and their fetches, prometheans and so forth. The Malleus Maleficarum would probably be able to bring a lot into the Church but they'd probably find their license to go around wherever they want hindered in certain places. The Ascended Ones would probably be targeted by ISIS and other extremists, and not be received by the other side very well either.<br /> <br /> I guess a lot would depend on how it happened and when it happened, but I believe eventually there would be a system in place for hunters, whether it involves simply absolving them of crimes due to technicalities or having them become part of some legally recognized militia with, ideally, a lot of oversight. That's just in America, though, and stuff would be crazy everywhere for a long time if the Masquerade was just torn down overnight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it so simple, given that Hunters aren't a &quot;type&quot;, but an activity.<br /> <br /> Some groups could come to the fore, more or less. TF-Valkyrie would probably be dismantled, not accepted. The idea of a conspiracy running for more than a century under a parallel set of ranks in the military isn't going to be well received, better just make it disappear. And them, a new official Task Force is created through the official canals, probably under another name to never be linked with old Valkyrie operations. If not dismantled, Valkyrie would remain occult, even if another TF operates officially. Each group would be a unique case.<br /> <br /> By the way, though the splats themselves are probable to become known, their organizations and societies are another matter entirely. They can adapt, be revealed, remain, split, transform or die in a case by case stance.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think most antagonistic groups are going to have an easier time. Belial's vampires are crazy homicidal cultists, VII is the business card of terrorists and serial-killers, the Pure aren't known for wanting to be on good terms with humanity. Only the Seers would really have it easier, but I'm not sure if all that easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-30-2015, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T10:46:54-07:00","id":645585,"title":"","content":"I think some of the organizations would become well known, for various reasons, while others stay obscure to anyone that isn't well read on the splats.<br /> <br /> For example, I imagine some Fire Touched family/pack might get their own &quot;religious family with way too many kids&quot; type show on TLC, thus bringing some fame and sympathy to the followers of Rabid Wolf. And maybe a couple of the younger kids that went through the first change at grade school age might be seen as being &quot;cute&quot; as far as werewolves go, but then have one of the older children get caught up in a scandal (as a result of a leak by Iron Master hackers) that blows what's going on with the Duggars right now out of the water.<br /> <br /> Oh my Gods, Fire Touched Duggars need to be a Pure pack in my next campaign!<br /> <br /> Basically any faction that would work well with an established TV show genre would probably be well known.<br /> <br /> EDIT: then again, maybe it would be more like that<span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt show on Netflix, a sitcom about a young former fire touched who escaped the tribe and is now trying to start a life for themselves among the forsaken of a big city far from her former tribe mates.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-30-2015, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T13:36:26-07:00","id":645840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=645210#post645210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it so simple, given that Hunters aren't a &quot;type&quot;, but an activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the activity is, outside of some exceptions, pretty much all the same. Hunting and killing supernaturals. If supernaturals are open to the public, they can call cops like the next person, providing cops will respond to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I don't think most antagonistic groups are going to have an easier time. Belial's vampires are crazy homicidal cultists, VII is the business card of terrorists and serial-killers, the Pure aren't known for wanting to be on good terms with humanity. Only the Seers would really have it easier, but I'm not sure if all that easy. </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I didn't say easier time, I said well received. Seers would be easily recruited by companies who want a tyrant that can squeeze every last dime out of people and guarantee they'd never utter a peep in complaint, or any military that wants soldiers who will do and die. Obviously not universally, but in the echelons of power you'd find people jumping at the chance to get Seers on their side. Especially considering how some of the Orders look in comparison. Secret police deciding who dies, a religion dedicated to knowledge who believe they're the only ones who can decide when it's okay to dole out, if at all, and the Silver Ladder whose mandate practically puts them at odds with every government on Earth.<br /> <br /> I also find it easy to imagine swaths of humanity that would find the Pure ideals exciting enough to try and, somehow, 'join up.' ISIS is doing it, and the Pure have a mindset that's much easier for people to appreciate than the Forsaken. 'We want to go back to a better time, honor your family, honor the spirit, honor the hunt,' are beliefs that are going to go a lot farther in modern day compared to the Forsaken's more arbitrary hunting-what-they-don't-like, which would get a lot of hate. An entire world opens up with the Shadow, and the Forsaken would still have to keep one side separate from the other. People would hate them, and that's not even factoring in first edition's 'spirit cop' idea.<br /> <br /> Angels would be much more acceptable to the masses, even governments. After all, they're keeping the universe in order, while demons are rogue agents who are only able to roam around on Earth doing what they want because they trade in souls and quantum wishes.<br /> <br /> The Brood aren't all crazy homicidal cultists, they could probably get away with claiming the Pandaemonium and Roaring Serpent as an extremist minority. But I wasn't referring to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=645585#post645585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, I imagine some Fire Touched family/pack might get their own &quot;religious family with way too many kids&quot; type show on TLC, thus bringing some fame and sympathy to the followers of Rabid Wolf. And maybe a couple of the younger kids that went through the first change at grade school age might be seen as being &quot;cute&quot; as far as werewolves go, but then have one of the older children get caught up in a scandal (as a result of a leak by Iron Master hackers) that blows what's going on with the Duggars right now out of the water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And with Predator Kings you have Bear Grylls taken to the extreme. With the Ivory Claws you have heirs and heiresses with drama and shapeshifting and magic. The Pure would probably dominate the reality show circuit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-30-2015, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T15:34:19-07:00","id":645956,"title":"","content":"I can't help but think that corporations would pointedly avoid hiring Seers, seeing as it would make them targets for Diamond and Free Council mages. I think they'd probably avoid the conflict entirely. I can't help but think that magic, Awakened or not, will probably quickly become industrialized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T15:46:59-07:00","id":645966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=645956#post645956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but think that corporations would pointedly avoid hiring Seers, seeing as it would make them targets for Diamond and Free Council mages. I think they'd probably avoid the conflict entirely. I can't help but think that magic, Awakened or not, will probably quickly become industrialized.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not so sure about that. What about Paradox, Lunacy, Vinculum and the like? Unless you want to rule that the Unveiling removes those phenomena or makes them insignificant, making a profit off your powers would be hard. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T15:52:22-07:00","id":645969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=645966#post645966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not so sure about that. What about Paradox, Lunacy, Vinculum and the like? Unless you want to rule that the Unveiling removes those phenomena or makes them insignificant, making a profit off your powers would be hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could hide the magic parts from non-magical end-users. Forces-Mind-enhanced servers, Fetish-based security systems, voluntary Embrace/Ghouling for wealthy clients, Changeling Pacts for beauty and strength in exchange for cold, hard cash, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T01:46:43-07:00","id":646446,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgists and Psychics, basically Mortal+, are far more likely to get hired than Mages.<br /> <br /> Why would a mage want to get hired?<br /> <br /> Any mage that cares about money has more than a few easy ways to get it anyway. Most probably don't care terribly much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T04:42:45-07:00","id":646548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=646446#post646446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumaturgists and Psychics, basically Mortal+, are far more likely to get hired than Mages.<br /> <br /> Why would a mage want to get hired?<br /> <br /> Any mage that cares about money has more than a few easy ways to get it anyway. Most probably don't care terribly much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seers, at least, instill tyranny. To be fair I guess they could just open a corporate retreat or training center for would-be executives where they could just alter their minds into becoming perfect tyrants or something. People would probably still go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:01:32-07:00","id":660763,"title":"","content":"Now I'm thinking, how would the Wod Revealed affect the music industry?<br /> <br /> I can't help but think that an altered version(s) of &quot;pretty fly for a white guy&quot; would be the anthem of supernaturals that are tired of dealing with mortal wannabes.<br /> <br /> Also, given the effects MTV had on the music industry in regard to putting sexiness in music videos over actual musical talent, how would the addition of illusion magic effect the music industry? I can't help but wonder if maybe musicians who normally wouldn't be attractive enough to get on MTV could use illusion magic to alter their appearance and allow some actual talent to get back in the industry?<br /> <br /> An all changeling rock band made up of musical kiths is something I would love to see. In fact, is their any chance that the music industry would be dominated by supernaturals and their various musical talents and abilities, or would magically enhanced music be looked at the same way people look at autotune?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:43:31-07:00","id":660806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=645210#post645210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some groups could come to the fore, more or less. TF-Valkyrie would probably be dismantled, not accepted. The idea of a conspiracy running for more than a century under a parallel set of ranks in the military isn't going to be well received, better just make it disappear. And them, a new official Task Force is created through the official canals, probably under another name to never be linked with old Valkyrie operations. If not dismantled, Valkyrie would remain occult, even if another TF operates officially. Each group would be a unique case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most (if not all) of Vigil's tier 3 groups do not want the public to know that the supernatural exists because then they then will have to answer for the atrocities that they have committed to over the life span of their operation.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T10:40:29-07:00","id":662042,"title":"","content":"If you want an idea of what a World of Darkness might look like without the Masquerade, you should have a look at the Mexican town of Catemaco. This video is 25 minutes long and is entirely in Spanish with subtitles, but it's interesting.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YKVlMMbTI9s\" data-code=\"YKVlMMbTI9s\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YKVlMMbTI9s/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T17:18:22-07:00","id":662427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=646548#post646548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Seers, at least, instill tyranny. To be fair I guess they could just open a corporate retreat or training center for would-be executives where they could just alter their minds into becoming perfect tyrants or something. People would probably still go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How many would know the difference? Or care?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=660763#post660763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An all changeling rock band made up of musical kiths is something I would love to see. In fact, is their any chance that the music industry would be dominated by supernaturals and their various musical talents and abilities, or would magically enhanced music be looked at the same way people look at autotune?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;In other news, the fairy band The Hedge mysteriously disappeared on tour today. Police are searching, and eyewitnesses claimed a 'man with thistle-down arms took the bus right off the road'. More details at 10.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changelings still need to worry about the Gentry, and mortal support isn't really going to make that much difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-12-2015, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T19:32:30-07:00","id":662548,"title":"","content":"To be honest, in a Revealed world, I don't think it would be too hard to get support for an all-out war on the Gentry (as hilariously one-sided as that would be in the Fair Folk's favor). They even have the &quot;foreign invaders stealing our children&quot; angle to work with. Even without that, it would be pretty easy for Changeling Courts to become recognized entities (consider them &quot;religious groups&quot;) with a great deal of protection and legal leeway. And if everything's unveiled, I don't think it would be too absurd to have a few Prometheans decide that humans stolen by the Gentry are worth saving. They're nearly invisible to the Gentry, hard as nails, and have a pretty wide bag of tricks, so if anyone is equipped to run recovery in Arcadia, it would be the Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T03:07:07-07:00","id":662861,"title":"","content":"Asfar as i can think, most of the Tier 1/2 Hunters would be headhunted for Police &quot;Experts&quot; on the various Supernatural types. Maybe as external &quot;Specialists&quot; or internal &quot;Department of Supernatural Affairs&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast would probably help set-up Support Groups for Heroes to help them understand what they are and how to &quot;Recover&quot; from it. I can Also see them/Some of them Setting up a Horror Theme Park or the Like... With Area's that lead into some of the Other Realms/Lairs set to look like the Realms. Hell... I Once Ran a Game that was basically that... &quot;Survive 7 days in the Park and get $1,000,000&quot;<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WjGD7IzDN8E&amp;list=PL760CE265680650B5\" target=\"_blank\">Also know as the Illbleed Scenario</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T09:50:44-07:00","id":663238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=645585#post645585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think some of the organizations would become well known, for various reasons, while others stay obscure to anyone that isn't well read on the splats.<br /> <br /> For example, I imagine some Fire Touched family/pack might get their own &quot;religious family with way too many kids&quot; type show on TLC, thus bringing some fame and sympathy to the followers of Rabid Wolf. And maybe a couple of the younger kids that went through the first change at grade school age might be seen as being &quot;cute&quot; as far as werewolves go, but then have one of the older children get caught up in a scandal (as a result of a leak by Iron Master hackers) that blows what's going on with the Duggars right now out of the water.<br /> <br /> Oh my Gods, Fire Touched Duggars need to be a Pure pack in my next campaign!<br /> <br /> Basically any faction that would work well with an established TV show genre would probably be well known.<br /> <br /> EDIT: then again, maybe it would be more like that<span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt show on Netflix, a sitcom about a young former fire touched who escaped the tribe and is now trying to start a life for themselves among the forsaken of a big city far from her former tribe mates.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well known is a tricky concept. Even with a TV show for them, what the public sees isn't necessarily most of their reality, unless you believe that TV shows are accurate depictions of reality. By the way, distinct TV shows can have wildly different takes on the same group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the activity is, outside of some exceptions, pretty much all the same. Hunting and killing supernaturals. If supernaturals are open to the public, they can call cops like the next person, providing cops will respond to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be precise: I think the activity of hunting supernaturals would be not only well known, but actually obvious to expect. Indeed, it would have at first its greatest surge of inductees of all time. A world of known supernatural will be a world where everyone have the most basic knowledge needed to make the decision to take the Vigil, so yes, everyone with the will to do so will act upon it, and you can expect a lot of people in this.<br /> <br /> But what isn't so simple are the groups themselves. First of all, because they are criminals, almost all of them. They are institutions of humans, so they are just common people that joined those groups and accepted to do their things. And them we have a long list of crimes. The simpler ones are just illegal watchers, doing police job, and sometimes executions, without state consent. The Conspiracies are all in dirtier mud. Cheiron Group does illegal research, Task Force Valkyrie is a paramilitary group leeching the resources of the Pentagon, and so on and so forth. Certainly some of them can get the upper hand on some scenarios, but they have simply too much to explain to simply go out.<br /> <br /> AND, of course... you can simply ignore your previous history, get your buddies and <u>pretend</u> that you are only now going in for the Vigil. But that isn't the same, because to go out in public means to make a lot of compromises, and those compromises depend on a lot of things. It isn't anymore just your intention toward the unknown. It is now also your intention toward the known and toward the society and its expectations. TFV would probably be dismantled because it is too much a liability, but it would be relatively simple to create internal procedures to absorb both its agents, its archives and its assets into the Pentagon proper and them simply create another, public, Task Force. But them, this new TF for dealing with the supernatural would have a change in policy to account for the new expectations created by the state of things. The end result will still be a Task Force in the US military with the resources to deal with supernatural threats. But how they perform this, or even their new definition of &quot;supernatural threat&quot; can be wildly distinct from the original TFV. And maybe the original TFV remains in the shadow precisely to keep their ways.<br /> <br /> Imagine this for each group of Hunters. Maybe the Union just become a political party who advocate for laws to protect against the supernatural. Maybe two, with extremists now having reason to left the main group (or a minority of non-extremists doing so). The Cheiron Group would have to find ways to legalize its discoveries quickly, before they lose the monopoly over supernatural research. Actually it works for supernatural groups, too. What changes about the Hunters is that with other splats you have one reception for the groups and other for the splat itself. For Hunters there are no &quot;splat itself&quot;, so only the destinies of the groups matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I didn't say easier time, I said well received.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, got it. I'm not sure the &quot;main&quot; groups aren't able to be as well received, though. I just think about some Storm Lords breaking a deal with Discovery for half a dozen shows. The Iron Masters would probably have an easier time making contact with human institutions, anyway, from the mob to the police, with Hollywood in the middle. For Uratha, I do think the Forsaken would have an easier time and be more well received, because they're more probable to simply keep to their human lives and from there carve their niche.<br /> <br /> Now that I thought about it, I think that who would really have better acceptance among human society would be the Ghost Wolves. And for Mages, the local minor Orders, not Seers nor Pentacle to be fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you could hide the magic parts from non-magical end-users. Forces-Mind-enhanced servers, Fetish-based security systems, voluntary Embrace/Ghouling for wealthy clients, Changeling Pacts for beauty and strength in exchange for cold, hard cash, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, welcome to the Sixth World, the setting of Shadowrun. Sooner or latter the supernatural will be integrated, and them the lines between supernatural societies among themselves and with human institutions will blur even more. The Seers can actually lose more in philosophical and religious terms as common (and ruthless) Corporations are more efficient at their game: profit, and hire people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings still need to worry about the Gentry, and mortal support isn't really going to make that much difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't be so sure, but indeed it raises a lot of questions. The Changelings are maybe the most probable to be accepted and helped by society, because they're first and foremost victims. And the mortal institutions are likely to throw a lot of their time and resources into the problem of the Gentry. Those are real threats, beings from another plane invading the world to take away its people. So, even if at first the mortal institutions don't have the means to protect them, to deal with the Gentry is probably going to be a high priority mission for most of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, in a Revealed world, I don't think it would be too hard to get support for an all-out war on the Gentry (as hilariously one-sided as that would be in the Fair Folk's favor). They even have the &quot;foreign invaders stealing our children&quot; angle to work with. Even without that, it would be pretty easy for Changeling Courts to become recognized entities (consider them &quot;religious groups&quot;) with a great deal of protection and legal leeway. And if everything's unveiled, I don't think it would be too absurd to have a few Prometheans decide that humans stolen by the Gentry are worth saving. They're nearly invisible to the Gentry, hard as nails, and have a pretty wide bag of tricks, so if anyone is equipped to run recovery in Arcadia, it would be the Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it isn't even as one-sided. First because the Fair Folk have as a rule that they can't overwhelm in a conflict. As veiled as it is, they need to always set an achievable winning condition for the other side. Second because with this unveiled world, information will spread. So each time someone finds a weapon against the Gentry, everyone knows it. Research teams will be able to actually make the statistical numbers and define among the suspicions of the Changelings what really can be true about the True Fae, or at least point a more sensible line of investigation. Not that humanity is always a cooperative bunch, but in such a case it is probable to become an effort of almost all of Earth institutions in cooperative research for means to defend our world.<br /> <br /> Just don't think the Courts are going to be like religions. Their primary purpose is to offer protection against the Gentry, and it is likely to be still the same. They could become the nexuses of the numerous Task Teams over the world committed to fight the &quot;Gentry Threat&quot;. An internal culture is already a common element on any organization, and they will still retain theirs, but with the new developments, it is impossible to know ahead of time how they will change internally. But overall they will be institutions for protection, research and fight against the Threats from the Gentry and their related Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T14:19:06-07:00","id":663479,"title":"","content":"The problem is one of logistics. The Fair Folk dwell in Arcadia, and travel through the Hedge, which is inhospitable and can open anywhere (near enough). You can't really invade their realms with any kind of real force. Normal people can't really strike <i>at</i> the Gentry, so it is basically a defense game against an enemy that can strike where-ever and when-ever they choose. And can spin up bargains with <i>reality</i> that can screw over what countermeasures you do put in place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T15:00:08-07:00","id":663502,"title":"","content":"Well, I wouldn't put it so simple. The enemy in question isn't one that can easily adapt, to begin with. Yes, they can strike bargains with reality. But are also bound by the same bargains. They are disorganized, crazy, and even their unpredictability comes from erratic behavior, not from clever strategy. They can have yet unknown weaknesses to be exploited. And even the problem with they dwelling in Arcadia can be overcome with Changeling help. Imagine what a group of Changelings can accomplish with backup from government, an actual job, access to therapy developed for helping with Clarity, real institutional support, intelligence and the resources an international operation can muster. And in the end, if they need it, the backup of mortal armies.<br /> <br /> After all, that new Task Force won't have to avoid contact with the supernatural. It will probably have some of them among their ranks, instead. One of the easiest ways for any supernatural being to be accept would probably be to work against this kind of threat. Imagine those Changelings eventually working with Vampires, Mages, Werewolves, Prometheans, Demons, Geists...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T15:26:01-07:00","id":663516,"title":"","content":"Is the Hedge impenetrable? If a changeling let a bunch of workers in could they burn it back in places where it was made of plants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T04:27:46-07:00","id":664093,"title":"","content":"Isn't it only metaphorically plant-like? I'd be pretty sure the Hedge would dislike such attempts to alter it so.<br /> <br /> As for leading a strike team to Arcadia, they'd have to be Changelings (or otherwise supernatural), or risk getting their Integrity shredded before long. The Fae Folk are likely more hindered by being &quot;sporting&quot;, than random inherent weaknesses. But if you step up the opposition, what becomes &quot;sporting&quot; changes to compensate. I just don't think additional support would really prevent all that many abductions. And the strain of such constant vigilance would probably scrap any large scale support before too long.<br /> <br /> But the break away from Changeling for a bit, how would the public accept Vampires, who pretty much need to cause some harm to exist, and can warp your mind, or Werewolves, who upon occasion <i>eat people</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:50:59-07:00","id":664541,"title":"","content":"Well, werewolves don't HAVE to eat people, and the oath says they're not supposed to, so maybe that would help with acceptance.<br /> <br /> As for vampires, it's only a matter of time before someone invents a blood substitute, or finds one that already existed that the vampires didn't know about (legends of vampire water melons that produce blood from the folklore of the Romani people might be notable here.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T11:30:35-07:00","id":664562,"title":"","content":"I believe there is a goblin fruit that provides 1 Vitae when consumed by a vampire, but I don't recall where it is. Massive industrialized goblin fruit farms would be interesting, if incredibly dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T11:34:53-07:00","id":664568,"title":"","content":"Every large company would hire spiritualists or werewolves to get in touch with their company's spirits to arrange for coordinated use of Aggressive Meme when starting new marketing campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T16:24:30-07:00","id":665039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=664568#post664568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every large company would hire spiritualists or werewolves to get in touch with their company's spirits to arrange for coordinated use of Aggressive Meme when starting new marketing campaigns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before the federal government shuts that down hard, because it's basically mind control. And once the world knows that mind control is a thing, it's going to be outlawed so hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T06:35:10-07:00","id":666932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=664562#post664562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there is a goblin fruit that provides 1 Vitae when consumed by a vampire, but I don't recall where it is. Massive industrialized goblin fruit farms would be interesting, if incredibly dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remember something saying that kind of thing is definitionally impossible, due to Hedge being mad or something? Don't quote me on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:15:33-07:00","id":667341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=665039#post665039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the federal government shuts that down hard, because it's basically mind control. And once the world knows that mind control is a thing, it's going to be outlawed so hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still gotta prove it, though. &quot;But a Vampire/Spirit mind-controlled me&quot; isn't all that different from hearing &quot;but the devil made me do it&quot; (leaving aside theological arguments).<br /> <br /> What <i>would</i> be the legal ramifications of Control vs Urging be? With Urging (and similar powers), you still have choice in what you are doing. Equivalent to duress, or could it be argued that it is no different from heckling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-16-2015, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:19:04-07:00","id":667344,"title":"","content":"Bloodroot is a story hook from the ST chapter of the Changeling corebook. It's a narcotic, not sustenance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:43:04-07:00","id":667368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=667341#post667341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still gotta prove it, though. &quot;But a Vampire/Spirit mind-controlled me&quot; isn't all that different from hearing &quot;but the devil made me do it&quot; (leaving aside theological arguments).<br /> <br /> What <i>would</i> be the legal ramifications of Control vs Urging be? With Urging (and similar powers), you still have choice in what you are doing. Equivalent to duress, or could it be argued that it is no different from heckling?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be impossible to control. At least bribes have a trail of money and services. A vampire just has to be in a room with someone in order to compromise them. A mage doesn't even require that, and a vampire with certain disciplines can get away with it as well. The governments of the world would be effectively powerless in the case of supernaturals going public until an arrangement was made for them that, ideally, prompted the supernaturals into going with the flow as much as possible. They could tack new laws but nothing could realistically enforce them except other supernaturals, and that's not something that would be guaranteed.<br /> <br /> Most of our laws work as a deterrent. If you get caught, you could get fined, you could be sent to jail and have your normal life ruined. But most supernaturals are already living lives that force them to avoid a normal life and hide from the law.. If you threaten a vampire with prison, or the Final Death, what's to keep them from just saying 'screw it,' turning on obfuscate and living like they did before the Masquerade fell, hidden and in the shadows? A werewolf can just find a new territory or escape into the Shadow until the heat dies down.<br /> <br /> I'm sure some governments could get away with something to pacify some of the supernaturals, like offering vampires 'All Access' passes to prisoners if, in exchange, they performed services for the government. But outside of governments like that I imagine the big power players on the human side would be corporations, who could offer money and comforts and services in exchange for services rendered. A corporation could grab up cold iron for changelings to keep their overseas transporting services low through Contracts, or the blood of donor employees and bought from Red Cross to vampires who helped their lobbyists in the halls of the government.<br /> <br /> This is wandering into the thoughts of the Scars thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-16-2015, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:42:32-07:00","id":667464,"title":"","content":"Well, a Mind Knowing spell from a Mage could detect mental influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T14:55:04-07:00","id":667470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=667464#post667464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a Mind Knowing spell from a Mage could detect mental influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the mages have their own agendas, ranging from the Silver Ladder's overthrowing all governments to put up their own and the Seers' grinding everyone beneath their masters' bootheel, I don't see them as someone who you could really trust. Even if you could find a trustworthy mage who is willing to, I suppose, detect mental influence on behalf of a government, as Vent0 pointed out there's the difference between control and urging, the need to pinpoint the specific occasion of the mental influence, track down the source of the influence, and all the way down the line you have a spirit, which doesn't come under government mandate to begin with. That's providing you can even track down the mental influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:02:25-07:00","id":667536,"title":"","content":"I think that they could come up with a test for seeing if someone was manipulated with mind control, maybe testing for special neurotransmitters that were created by the mind control magic (my head canon is that mind control magic works by creating a combination of neurotransmitters that creates the desired effect) or something like that, or else a magical test? And besides, someone people who suffer from certain mental illnesses would probably find mind control to be a useful means of helping manage their mental illness. I have some serious bi-polar/temper issues on top of my autism and if I could pay a vampire or a mage to hack my mind so that my temper was less of a problem I would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:18:22-07:00","id":667544,"title":"","content":"Mage expert witnesses. &quot;According to my expert opinion as a Master of the Mind Arcanum, the person was <i>not</i> mind-controlled.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't know why, but this makes me laugh <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:08:16-07:00","id":667617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=667536#post667536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that they could come up with a test for seeing if someone was manipulated with mind control, maybe testing for special neurotransmitters that were created by the mind control magic (my head canon is that mind control magic works by creating a combination of neurotransmitters that creates the desired effect) or something like that, or else a magical test?</div> </div> </div> </div>They certainly could. But then all you'd have to do to disqualify a candidate you didn't like from becoming president was, during a moment when they weren't being watched, have them drop a cup and now they would test positive for being influenced with magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And besides, someone people who suffer from certain mental illnesses would probably find mind control to be a useful means of helping manage their mental illness. I have some serious bi-polar/temper issues on top of my autism and if I could pay a vampire or a mage to hack my mind so that my temper was less of a problem I would. </div> </div> </div>I have my own issues, but I wouldn't trust a vampire or mage to deal with them. I don't want to find myself offering my blood every Thursday night without knowing why, or paradox in my brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T22:38:23-07:00","id":667835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=667617#post667617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> paradox in my brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just a couple spiders. You'll hardly notice them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T13:23:18-07:00","id":681348,"title":"","content":"Thought of throwing this in here because supernatural guy and Tumblr.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_NlQJYvBVq8\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_NlQJYvBVq8\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_NlQJYvBVq8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/_NlQJYvBVq8 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This guy's an Acanthus mage and yes, Tyler Dawn is his Sympathetic Name. He has a Shadow Name, too. Cypher. But he doesn't use it...<br /> <br /> Speaking of Nic Cage, I'm convinced that he's a mage as well. Fame's a pretty decent sympathetic defense, and he's probably using a screen name as a Shadow Name. Why do you think he got the part for Sorcerer's Apprentice? The Lie told you it was special effects.<br /> <br /> He uses magic to make his films the greatest thing you've ever seen, but since that's an obvious magical effect done around Sleepers witnesses, it risks Paradox. But Nic's a nice mage, so he contains it in his pattern, causing Bedlam, which the ignorant herd sees as his &quot;moments&quot;. Besides, the last time he didn't contain it resulted in a Manifestation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-1GadTfGFvU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-1GadTfGFvU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-1GadTfGFvU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/-1GadTfGFvU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Those were Abyssal bees...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:08:51-07:00","id":681389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=681348#post681348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Nic Cage, I'm convinced that he's a mage as well. Fame's a pretty decent sympathetic defense, and he's probably using a screen name as a Shadow Name. Why do you think he got the part for Sorcerer's Apprentice? The Lie told you it was special effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, his actual name is Nic Coppola, so I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T11:05:21-07:00","id":684654,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea I just had. What would networks like the History Channel and Nat Geo be like in the WoD revealed? The history channel in particular has been moving away from history and into the paranormal, but in the WoD revealed there's no reason the programming couldn't combine the two. In fact, given that many supernaturals are quite long lived, there's no reason they couldn't have shows where they interview supernaturals that were actually there for the events. I'm pretty sure that the fog of eternity isn't in 2e vampire, and Werewolves can live for a long time if nothing kills them. Add in the arisen and various other splats and history documentaries would be awesome again.<br /> <br /> And that is how you do Dark Eras flashbacks in the WoD revealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T20:21:49-07:00","id":685167,"title":"","content":"History Channel: What's history like today after the latest Supernal rewrite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link"