 subject of a Disney movie, with themed areas around each of those movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T15:41:39-07:00","id":926111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=926094#post926094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is right before some <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\">Thyrsus</span></span> </span>working for Disney creates their newest theme park &quot;Disney's Pleasure Island&quot; in the Mediterranean. It quickly expands from donkeys into animal transformations of every animal types that has ever been the subject of a Disney movie, with themed areas around each of those movies.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i1.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/710/416/6c6.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T05:27:43-07:00","id":927565,"title":"","content":"I'm being kept awake by that moment when you remember the propensity Werewolves and Changing Breeds have for ending up in romantic relationships with the animals they turn into, and connect it with Neo-Reactionaryism's propensity to defend pretty much every group they see as persecuted. I feel like the PC crowd would explode if they realised the implications of people who are also animals sometimes deciding that they prefer to date on the non-human side....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T08:04:33-07:00","id":927623,"title":"","content":"That's more of a Werewolf the Apocalypse thing. I don't think it pops up in Changeling the Lost at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T08:21:12-07:00","id":927627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927565#post927565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm being kept awake by that moment when you remember the propensity Werewolves and Changing Breeds have for ending up in romantic relationships with the animals they turn into, and connect it with Neo-Reactionaryism's propensity to defend pretty much every group they see as persecuted. I feel like the PC crowd would explode if they realised the implications of people who are also animals sometimes deciding that they prefer to date on the non-human side....</div> </div> </div> </div>As part of &quot;the PC crowd&quot;... No. If there were people who could shapeshift into animals, it wouldn't make it ok for them to have sexual relationships with animals. Their ability to take animal form doesn't change the animal's inability to consent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:08:23-07:00","id":927689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927565#post927565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm being kept awake by that moment when you remember the propensity Werewolves and Changing Breeds have for ending up in romantic relationships with the animals they turn into, and connect it with Neo-Reactionaryism's propensity to defend pretty much every group they see as persecuted. I feel like the PC crowd would explode if they realised the implications of people who are also animals sometimes deciding that they prefer to date on the non-human side....</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha must produce with humans- or, as of 2e, can produce Wolfblooded with other werewolves. Garou could mate with wolves, which was one of the parts of Apocalypse that made me shy away with it. And the less I think about Changing Breeds, the better. That book was chock-full of uncomfortable implications and off-putting content.<br /> <br /> Long story short, sexual acts, in order to be consensual, require the knowing participation and consent of both parties. Animals are incapable of giving consent, since they are incapable of making rational decisions or, you know, intelligent human speech. Garou, even though they are capable of reproducing with wolves, would still be up to their eyeballs in hot water. Uratha, who have no reason to mate with wolves at all, would be even worse off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 07-07-2016, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:10:15-07:00","id":927690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927565#post927565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm being kept awake by that moment when you remember the propensity Werewolves and Changing Breeds have for ending up in romantic relationships with the animals they turn into, and connect it with Neo-Reactionaryism's propensity to defend pretty much every group they see as persecuted. I feel like the PC crowd would explode if they realised the implications of people who are also animals sometimes deciding that they prefer to date on the non-human side....</div> </div> </div> </div>As another member of the PC crowd, I second what Charlaquin said: bestiality is an issue of consent and animal rights, and human-born shapeshifters don't magically get the right to determine that sort of thing to justify criminal acts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:30:48-07:00","id":927705,"title":"","content":"&quot;Just because you've got the parts, it doesn't matter if they don't have the smarts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Taking the conversation back towards humorous: how well do you think the &quot;no pets allowed&quot; signs would be taken in a world with shapeshifters and familiars?<br /> <br /> More Seriously: How would incarceration and punishment laws change? You pretty much can't really hold Mages. It's cruel towards (many?) Changelings, on account of Clarity trauma. What does a life sentence even mean for Vampires. A Death Sentence is counter-productive with Sin-Eaters. Let alone the nightmares the legal and justice systems would face with the whole can of worms the Unchained open up (considering they can retroactively alter <i>who</i> committed a crime with Pacts, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:41:00-07:00","id":927713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927690#post927690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another member of the PC crowd, I second what Charlaquin said: bestiality is an issue of consent and animal rights, and human-born shapeshifters don't magically get the right to determine that sort of thing to justify criminal acts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, even animal-born shapeshifters (if they exist in what ever version of the setting is being revealed here) generally gain more or less human-like intelligence and consciousness, which in my book carries with it the responsibility to obtain a partner's consent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:42:46-07:00","id":927716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927705#post927705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Just because you've got the parts, it doesn't matter if they don't have the smarts.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Taking the conversation back towards humorous: how well do you think the &amp;quot;no pets allowed&amp;quot; signs would be taken in a world with shapeshifters and familiars?<br /> <br /> More Seriously: How would incarceration and punishment laws change? You pretty much can't really hold Mages. It's cruel towards (many?) Changelings, on account of Clarity trauma. What does a life sentence even mean for Vampires. A Death Sentence is counter-productive with Sin-Eaters. Let alone the nightmares the legal and justice systems would face with the whole can of worms the Unchained open up (considering they can retroactively alter <i>who</i> committed a crime with Pacts, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>As of 2e, you can't really incarcerate Changelings either, unless you also starve them of Glamour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:08:06-07:00","id":927725,"title":"","content":"To be fair, vampires and werewolves at least can talk to animals and, I suppose, obtain consent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:23:33-07:00","id":927735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927725#post927725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, vampires and werewolves at least can talk to animals and, I suppose, obtain consent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adults can talk to children but they can't obtain consent from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T13:32:46-07:00","id":927761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927735#post927735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adults can talk to children but they can't obtain consent from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real question here is: does anybody really want to play a character who engages in bestiality, or have a ST character who engages in bestiality, in their Chronicles? No? Then let's <i>please </i>drop this line of thought and get back to more enjoyable discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T21:28:23-07:00","id":927959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927689#post927689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uratha must produce with humans- or, as of 2e, can produce Wolfblooded with other werewolves. Garou could mate with wolves, which was one of the parts of Apocalypse that made me shy away with it. And the less I think about Changing Breeds, the better. That book was chock-full of uncomfortable implications and off-putting content.<br /> <br /> Long story short, sexual acts, in order to be consensual, require the knowing participation and consent of both parties. Animals are incapable of giving consent, since they are incapable of making rational decisions or, you know, intelligent human speech. Garou, even though they are capable of reproducing with wolves, would still be up to their eyeballs in hot water. Uratha, who have no reason to mate with wolves at all, would be even worse off.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly one of the devs or writers has mentioned that Uratha can breed with wolves and end up with wolf blooded wolves who can experience the first change.<br /> <br /> Edit: Memory was a bit foggy. I was remember this post (<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken</a>) by Stew where he updated the Urhanu from the translation guide to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3323,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","user":"cmwatford","date":". 07-08-2016, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T23:08:14-07:00","id":927977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927959#post927959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly one of the devs or writers has mentioned that Uratha can breed with wolves and end up with wolf blooded wolves who can experience the first change.<br /> <br /> Edit: Memory was a bit foggy. I was remember this post (<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken</a>) by Stew where he updated the Urhanu from the translation guide to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>The translation guide offers rules for bringing over aspects of Apocalypse into Forsaken, and the other way around. One of the books actually has mentioned that this is a dead end, as werewolves are not wolves, or even part wolf, they are part human and part spirit of the hunt. Nevertheless, people want to bring 'regular' wolves into it, whether by enhancing them to Apocalypse's 'lupus' breed, with all the social interaction that may entail, or by bringing them into the pack.<br /> <br /> A more appropriate partner for sex, aside from the obvious humans and werewolves, would be spirits. Presumably it's another dead end. I imagine we'll find out when we hear more about the Fire-Touched.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I'd have animals be the mental equivalent of children, beyond young animals. I imagine a more Jungle Book, the book not the movie, style of things.<br /> <br /> What would be the reaction if, with this Masquerade fallen, some revealed they actually could speak to animals and them back? I don't think there would be a huge turn towards vegetarianism. But things would become further confusing when it was revealed that the spirits of cows and plants basically want to be eaten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-08-2016, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:44:03-07:00","id":928117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=927977#post927977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I'd have animals be the mental equivalent of children, beyond young animals. I imagine a more Jungle Book, the book not the movie, style of things.<br /> <br /> What would be the reaction if, with this Masquerade fallen, some revealed they actually could speak to animals and them back? I don't think there would be a huge turn towards vegetarianism. But things would become further confusing when it was revealed that the spirits of cows and plants basically want to be eaten.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we have different interpretations of what animal speech would be like. I've thought that if we could speak with animals, they would speak in short phrases. And except for great apes, I don't think animals would be able to communicate complex ideas and emotions, and anything that was beyond an animal's comprehension. So, if you asked a bird to do some surveillance work for you, and check if anybody entered or left a building, it wouldn't come back and say, &quot;After sundown, five men with visible tattoos and carrying firearms entered the building. There was a prolonged period of gunshots, and then the men left.&quot; It would probably something more like, &quot;Sun go down. Group of male humans. Markings and thunder sticks. Enter den. Lots of thunder. Then they leave.&quot; So, not something that's going to be able to debate the meaning of life with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T08:17:28-07:00","id":928147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=928117#post928117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess we have different interpretations of what animal speech would be like. I've thought that if we could speak with animals, they would speak in short phrases. And except for great apes, I don't think animals would be able to communicate complex ideas and emotions, and anything that was beyond an animal's comprehension. So, if you asked a bird to do some surveillance work for you, and check if anybody entered or left a building, it wouldn't come back and say, &quot;After sundown, five men with visible tattoos and carrying firearms entered the building. There was a prolonged period of gunshots, and then the men left.&quot; It would probably something more like, &quot;Sun go down. Group of male humans. Markings and thunder sticks. Enter den. Lots of thunder. Then they leave.&quot; So, not something that's going to be able to debate the meaning of life with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Jungle Book is more between the two. 'Man came with guns, they killed Man in den, then left.' Numbers aren't known, all humans are Man, they know what guns are because of the danger they pose but a tattoo wouldn't be a significant enough difference to note, and obviously know death when they see it. There would be a confusion of values, as well. Father Wolf, in the Jungle Book, notices Mowgli isn't afraid of him despite the fact that Father Wolf can kill him, and confuses this ignorance of the danger for bravery. A lot of variance in the views depending on the type of animal and its experience, a person's loyal hunting dog would be different than a 'wild' wolf from a pack which would be different from a wolf that has lived in a zoo all its life.<br /> <br /> And while they could argue the meaning of life, it would be based on said animal's experience and what it was taught by its own kind, not one gathered from many faraway cultures via books. It's not as if every person thinks the meaning of life is more complicated, there's plenty of cultures that boil it down to a simple phrase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-08-2016, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:31:59-07:00","id":928430,"title":"","content":"Is this whole mess because of my Disney's pleasure island comment? because while I wasn't thinking about the sex part, I would have thought that any sex on the resort would be between consenting humans turned into animals by the magi running the island ( I am assuming the shape shifted humans would be able understand each other while shifted, as a result of the mage spending a bit of reach).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T01:41:48-07:00","id":928643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=928430#post928430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this whole mess because of my Disney's pleasure island comment? because while I wasn't thinking about the sex part</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's an odd thought which was repeating in my head in the middle of the night, which people are taking in very different ways than what I meant to say.<br /> <br /> I will note that I think you guys might be missing the perspective those books are throwing down: they're pretty clear about the mindset of the &quot;healthy&quot; shapeshifter. A Were-Owl might find it perfectly natural to spend a large amount of time in Owl form, living life as an Owl rather than a human because it just appeals to them more, and while effectively living the life of an Owl, might end up with another Owl when mating season comes around, and have that relationship. From the perspective of non-were society, yes, this is going to be odd, but from their perspective it makes sense: they're both human AND nahaul, and sometimes they see the world from the nahaul perspective.<br /> <br /> Someone else mentioned the problematic propensity for Werewolves on the Spirit end of the harmony scale to interbreed with spirits, and that's a similar concept. I pulled that in the campaign I ran when I first got Werewolf 2E, where I had NPCs who were lost pack members, and they found out that their Occultist had not only been sharing notes on Werewolves with non-Uratha occultists, but had been having a secret affair with a spirit named Sunning Fox. They found out because they met a young spirit named Wolf in the Shade. They were perturbed by this as was my intention, especially when the guardian spirit their pack was working with told them how bad of a sign that was for Lucino's mental health. They didn't guess he'd gone full Bale Hound to an Idigam until it he'd set their shrine on fire though. This campaign, by the way, had a Lupine-origin Uratha, because I like Apocalypse too, and one player really wanted to play that: the story that I didn't tell her was that one of the leaders of the nearby Predator Kings had a similar set of markings, because he was the wolf's grandfather.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a complete tangent though. The original thought was really &quot;wouldn't we see some very odd reactions if humanity found that there was a whole group of people who shapeshift into, hold conversations with, and occasionally form those kinds of relationships and even breed with non human animals, and when confronted on it, say that it's natural for them because they are that animal.&quot; It also occurred to me that Tumblr would see a few people defending them. That was what I was trying to say, and as I explained, their actions have nuance to them that I think isn't coming across when you look at it from the perspective of western culture. especially when most of the mythology that book is written on is based in old American, Celtic, and Eastern mythology and mindsets, as well as from the perspective of people who literally think like the animals they turn into...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-09-2016, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T05:43:57-07:00","id":928701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=928643#post928643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note that I think you guys might be missing the perspective those books are throwing down: they're pretty clear about the mindset of the &quot;healthy&quot; shapeshifter. A Were-Owl might find it perfectly natural to spend a large amount of time in Owl form, living life as an Owl rather than a human because it just appeals to them more, and while effectively living the life of an Owl, might end up with another Owl when mating season comes around, and have that relationship. From the perspective of non-were society, yes, this is going to be odd, but from their perspective it makes sense: they're both human AND nahaul, and sometimes they see the world from the nahaul perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>What books are you talking about here? Is this a Changing Breeds thing? Changing Breeds is pretty generally disliked among the fan base for a lot of reasons, and this &quot;it's healthy for shapeshifters to live and sometimes mate with animals&quot; idea is not the least of them. Werewolf, on the other hand, takes completely the opposite stance on this. Uratha are <i>not</i> human and wolf, they are neither. They are Uratha. And it's <i>not</i> healthy for them to live as wolves, just like it's not healthy for them to live exclusively as humans, either will take a toll on Harmony.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=928643#post928643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone else mentioned the problematic propensity for Werewolves on the Spirit end of the harmony scale to interbreed with spirits, and that's a similar concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't exactly call it a propensity. It's not even really something that the books go into happening. I don't doubt that it does sometimes, but it's not like it's a common or accepted thing in werewolf society, in fact I imagine most Storm Lords and most Ivory Claws would find the idea disgusting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=928643#post928643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a complete tangent though. The original thought was really &quot;wouldn't we see some very odd reactions if humanity found that there was a whole group of people who shapeshift into, hold conversations with, and occasionally form those kinds of relationships and even breed with non human animals, and when confronted on it, say that it's natural for them because they are that animal.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, people would have odd reactions to the realization that there are people who can turn into animals, that's kind of a key point of the thread. No, it's not natural for shapeshifters to breed with animals, because they are <i>not</i> the animals they can turn into. In most cases, they are people who can become shaped like animals (hence the term <i>shape</i>shifter), and in the case of werewolves, they're neither, they're Pangaeans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=928643#post928643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also occurred to me that Tumblr would see a few people defending them. That was what I was trying to say, and as I explained, their actions have nuance to them that I think isn't coming across when you look at it from the perspective of western culture. especially when most of the mythology that book is written on is based in old American, Celtic, and Eastern mythology and mindsets, as well as from the perspective of people who literally think like the animals they turn into...</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course Tumblr would have people defending them, it's a huge website and it has people defending literally anything you can think of. The problem is that you lumped the people who would defend shapeshifters having sex with animals as part of &quot;the PC crowd&quot;, implying first of all that &quot;the PC crowd&quot; is a homogenous group, and second of all that this group would support what is essentially bestiality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:22:24-07:00","id":928759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=928701#post928701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't exactly call it a propensity. It's not even really something that the books go into happening. I don't doubt that it does sometimes, but it's not like it's a common or accepted thing in werewolf society, in fact I imagine most Storm Lords and most Ivory Claws would find the idea disgusting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah as far as I know it only happened once in a piece of fiction and even then was just a rumor and the protagonist thought it was an example of the character's corruption.<br /> <br /> I was just saying that it should be more of a concern than bestiality with wolves, as werewolves are not part wolf, they are part spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:50:02-07:00","id":928773,"title":"","content":"Well I just found something that would be of interest to some supernaturals in the CofD revealed, the Zone of Death in <a href=\"http://www.vox.com/2014/5/22/5738756/you-can-kill-someone-in-a-section-of-yellowstone-and-get-away-scot\" target=\"_blank\">Yellowstone National Park. </a><br /> Basically it is a 50 mile section of yellowstone where all crime is legal thanks to a loophole in the 6th amendment.<br /> <br /> So, how long would it be before it becomes something of an amusement park for the nastier supernaturals, where they can kill dumb teenagers to their black hearts' content with no interference from mortal authorities. I imagine the Yellowstone death zone is built like a small town with all the classic small town horror settings in it, including the cabin in the woods, the insane asylum, the high school, etc. The dumb teenagers that come to the town to play the victims are lured in with the promise of a great reward for the survivors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:49:11-07:00","id":928815,"title":"","content":"I do hate to be a buzzkill, but it seems less of an area where all crime is legal than one where jurisdiction is disputed. Odds are if a crime more serious than killing a deer was committed the 'loophole' would be closed up quickly.<br /> <br /> Similar to the concept of 'international waters,' it's not a place where you can do anything, just one where it's hard to claim where a crime happened, so who should deal with it, and different countries have different laws.<br /> <br /> Until then, there's federal park police who can deal with it.<br /> <br /> I always found the legal status of the undead to be more of an odd situation. Wealthy companies or families could put their money in the name a vampire they keep staked in a vault somewhere forever and never have to worry about losing it at death. Currently they have to waste lawyer feeds moving it around through fake foundations and shell companies.<br /> <br /> Plus Supreme Court positions are for life. With the various forms of immortality things start to become unchanging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-09-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T11:28:17-07:00","id":928829,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the supreme court thing would be fixed by making it so that a supreme court appointment is for a mortal lifetime. A supernatural being that lives longer would only serve for a period equal to how long a mortal justice would live. OF course I want to know how the supernatural would effect the drug trade and the culture surrounding it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T13:26:23-07:00","id":928888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=928815#post928815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hate to be a buzzkill, but it seems less of an area where all crime is legal than one where jurisdiction is disputed. Odds are if a crime more serious than killing a deer was committed the 'loophole' would be closed up quickly.<br /> <br /> Similar to the concept of 'international waters,' it's not a place where you can do anything, just one where it's hard to claim where a crime happened, so who should deal with it, and different countries have different laws.<br /> <br /> Until then, there's federal park police who can deal with it.<br /> <br /> I always found the legal status of the undead to be more of an odd situation. Wealthy companies or families could put their money in the name a vampire they keep staked in a vault somewhere forever and never have to worry about losing it at death. Currently they have to waste lawyer feeds moving it around through fake foundations and shell companies.<br /> <br /> Plus Supreme Court positions are for life. With the various forms of immortality things start to become unchanging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Supreme Court positions are also only held &quot;in good behavior&quot;, and most of the ways in which one becomes immortal in the WoD necessitate some pretty nasty things, either by the process, or by maintaining it. It's a flimsy clause, but it might be one way to oust a Vampire Justice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:00:28-07:00","id":929308,"title":"","content":"I'll tell you one thing for sure <br /> <br /> Whoever invents a camera that perfectly captures vampires is gonna be rich as fuck","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:44:22-07:00","id":929336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=929308#post929308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll tell you one thing for sure <br /> <br /> Whoever invents a camera that perfectly captures vampires is gonna be rich as fuck</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T14:05:25-07:00","id":929374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=929336#post929336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, considering the stuff TFV and Cheiron have built...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T14:08:43-07:00","id":929376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=929374#post929374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, considering the stuff TFV and Cheiron have built...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... I'm really hoping Hunter 2e moves away from breaking other gamelines' rules, but point taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:11:15-07:00","id":929403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=929376#post929376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... I'm really hoping Hunter 2e moves away from breaking other gamelines' rules, but point taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not super sure it counts as breaking a rule? There are plenty of things within Vampire that break the rules of vampirism, even specifically the mirrors and cameras one. Restored Image, for example. The Galloi could make a ton of cash if they found a way to mass-produce the effect. And given what the Ordo Dracul could do, making a vampire-adapted camera would probably be easy for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:17:09-07:00","id":929409,"title":"","content":"They don't blur and distort anymore anyways. Based off what we know of vampire powers, it seems like the vampire's aura works to muffle surveillance while the Beast guides them to the right position to be in.<br /> <br /> If someone built vampire aura proof technology it would have much better use in making users immune to most of their powers.<br /> <br /> In keeping with the tumblr concept, vampires blogs with selfies and pictures of friends would be fairly exclusive, as it wasn't anyone could just emulate with their cellphone.<br /> <br /> Would werewolves and mages be banned from such sites, as images of their magic could cause mental harm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-10-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:30:49-07:00","id":929417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=929409#post929409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't blur and distort anymore anyways. Based off what we know of vampire powers, it seems like the vampire's aura works to muffle surveillance while the Beast guides them to the right position to be in.<br /> <br /> If someone built vampire aura proof technology it would have much better use in making users immune to most of their powers.<br /> <br /> In keeping with the tumblr concept, vampires blogs with selfies and pictures of friends would be fairly exclusive, as it wasn't anyone could just emulate with their cellphone.<br /> <br /> Would werewolves and mages be banned from such sites, as images of their magic could cause mental harm?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the Revealed version of ChronDark, not default, so things like the Masquerade, Lunacy, and Quiescence wouldn't blur or muffle surveillance or strip memories of events (they'd probably still traumatize mortals, though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T17:20:45-07:00","id":929461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=929409#post929409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would werewolves and mages be banned from such sites, as images of their magic could cause mental harm?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be really hard to enforce. I think more likely, depictions of Supernal magic and/or Lunacy-triggering scenes would probably be against the ToS of most social media sites. Those that allowed it would probably highly encourage posters of such depictions to tag them so Sleepers and non-Wolf Blooded can filter them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T17:58:29-07:00","id":929469,"title":"","content":"#werewolf #milf #abs #fitness #breaking point<br /> <br /> I can dig it.<br /> <br /> I keep thinking of the harsher ramifications, the complete inability of any national security to even pretend to themselves secure, the fear of the common person overwhelming them, the new brands of discrimination. Finding it harder to go lighter and imagine Mummies teaching classes of anthropology and starting online scavenger hunts to look for relics or changelings offering tours of the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T02:19:04-07:00","id":929628,"title":"","content":"How long before the first Broadway musical with an all supernatural cast? For some reason I keep imagining a musical by Weird Al about corporate werewolves in the 80 and 90s called &quot;Dog eat Dog&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","va