":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T09:38:10-07:00","id":930382,"title":"","content":"My wife says she thinks werewolves haven't taken off like vampires have is because once they start shifting it's hard to keep them sexy. Vampire Tom Cruise and vampire Brad Pitt are still Tom Cruise and Brad Pitt. Taylor Lautner turning into a werewolf is suddenly unrecognizable as a human being, or might turn into something more reminiscent of a dog.<br /> <br /> I always thought Forsaken's Abrar Ajmal kept dalu looking pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:13:32-07:00","id":930429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=930380#post930380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that there has been only one good vampire musical (at least according to TV tropes), thus why the werewolves would take over Broadway</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how much I agree with that claim. There's so much politics around what constitutes a good musical. Bad blood makes people ignore Frank Wildhorn for basically no reason, and many of his musicals are really, really great (Bonnie and Clyde, anyone?). And then some people somehow categorize Andrew Lloyd Webber with the likes of Sondheim.<br /> <br /> I liked Lestat a lot. It wasn't its time, so it didn't work. Even five years later, it would have been much different.<br /> <br /> Dance of the Vampires wasn't great in the US, but Tanz der Vampire is amazing. With a different director, with a different budget, if they hadn't made it so campy, or if they made it now, it would have been much different.<br /> <br /> Twilight the Musical is a great spoof musical, and Meghann Fahy is actually amazing.<br /> <br /> I don't know if you consider Batboy a vampire musical. I do. Again, hilarious and great, in my humble opinion.<br /> <br /> Point is, vampire narratives come about during periods of historical transition. That's been the same since Polidori. Lestat didn't work in 2006. It would work now. And vampire musicals would certainly work after vampires literally revealed themselves to the public.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:20:47-07:00","id":930433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=930380#post930380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that there has been only one good vampire musical (at least according to TV tropes), thus why the werewolves would take over Broadway</div> </div> </div> </div>(Also, you're totally more than welcome to disagree with me, but shameless plug--I've been involved in theater since I was extremely young, and I went to an arts camp in Upstate New York to train with Broadway directors. Here's a video of myself singing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u3GNF-4O9CE\" data-code=\"u3GNF-4O9CE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/u3GNF-4O9CE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I also have studied vampires at high academic levels. I wrote an article applying Lacan's theories to <i>The Vampire Lestat</i> that I'm currently submitting to academic journals, I and took a class as an undergrad called Vampire Narratives. A few months ago, some people asked for the syllabus, and I shared it, if you're curious.<br /> <br /> I'm no longer pursuing professional work in theater, and I'm not a cultural historian, I'm a social historian, and I'm not by any means putting this down to say I KNOW ALL AND NO ONE ELSE SHOULD COMMENT, I just wanted to share my qualifications to kind of situate the debate. And shamelessly to get more hits on Youtube. Okay, moving on.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:41:52-07:00","id":930446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=929376#post929376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... I'm really hoping Hunter 2e moves away from breaking other gamelines' rules, but point taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to terrify innocent supernaturals by bypassing their defenses is part of the fun though: if the Faeries couldn't get Hunters to drag Changelings back to them in shackles they can no longer use their powers to escape, if the Demons can't get Hunters to set up dead zones where the Werewolves can't fight them, if the Seers can't get Hunters to Lobotomize the Adamantine Arrow operatives before they can save the city, how will the Hunters destroy what goods left in the World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> Tongue in cheek, of course, but being able to subvert other books is part of the appeal. Also, do they REALLY break the rules, or is it that they have access to things that aren't in those books? I mean, the Vampires in Night Stalkers are, for the most part, not Kindred...<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: oh wow, when I opened that and started writing, I didn't think there'd be 2 pages of discussion before I managed to post it 12 hours later...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T12:54:16-07:00","id":930481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr?p=930025#post930025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind for werewolves 'big game' gets a bit bigger.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i813.photobucket.com/albums/zz56/